<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cao Wei</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Wei dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cao Wei, or the Wei dynasty, was the state founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-pi">Cao Pi</a> in 220 CE after he deposed the last Han emperor. It controlled northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/three-kingdoms-period">Three Kingdoms period</a>, competing with Shu Han and Eastern Wu. Its founding marked the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cao-wei.jpg" alt="Cao Wei" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Three_Kingdoms.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
